# Correction Q1: No, the previous render only shows the torso moving up while the arm remains static. The core action of the arm contracting to flex the bicep is completely missing.
# Correction Q2: The entire sequence should be changed to show the flexing motion. It should start with the arm slightly extended outward, then transition sharply into the final flexed pose (arm bent, fist near shoulder, torso raised, and head turned to look at the bicep), and hold that final pose.
# Q1: How would a human perform this motion? A human would raise their arm to the side, then sharply bend the elbow to bring their fist towards their shoulder, tensing the bicep muscle.
# Q2: Pose Candidates Comparison. Candidate A: Start with arm extended outward (`arm_position: "out", elbow_bended: false`). Candidate B: Start with arm already bent (`arm_position: "in", elbow_bended: true`). Winner is A, as it provides a clear "wind-up" that makes the subsequent flexing motion more dramatic and understandable.
# Q3: Structure Comparison. M1: `pose` (start) -> `movement` (arm/torso joints) -> `pose` (hold). M2: `pose` (start) -> `pose` (final flexed pose with a long hold). Winner is M2 because it defines the start and end states clearly, creating a single, powerful, coordinated transition that includes the arm flex, torso lift, and head turn, which is more reliable than authoring complex multi-joint movements.
# Q4: Context Reinforcement. The best way to reinforce strength is to make the transition from the wind-up pose to the final flexed pose feel sharp and decisive. By defining the torso lift (`torso_height: "high"`) and head turn (`head: "right"`) within the final pose, these actions occur simultaneously with the arm flex, creating a single, impactful "power-up" moment. A hold time of ~1.5s allows the pose to register.
{
  "cue": "flex_bicep",
  "description": "The robot brings its arm out and then sharply contracts it to flex its bicep, simultaneously raising its torso and turning its head to admire the muscle.",
  "movements": [
    {
      "type": "pose",
      "duration": 0.5,
      "parameters": {
        "pose": {
          "torso_height": "mid",
          "arm_position": "out",
          "gripper_orientation": "vertical",
          "head": "center",
          "left_arm": "still",
          "elbow_bended": false,
          "z": 50,
          "y": 30
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "pose",
      "duration": 1.5,
      "parameters": {
        "pose": {
          "torso_height": "high",
          "arm_position": "in",
          "gripper_orientation": "vertical",
          "head": "right",
          "left_arm": "still",
          "elbow_bended": true,
          "z": 80,
          "y": 75
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
